  "orthographicCaveat": "Every arc fit here assumes an orthographic camera. The reference is a perspective render, which is why the belt's arc could not be fitted at all: its left and right extreme meridians, which an orthographic camera puts on the same image row, sit ~77 px apart. Radii read as horizontal extents are unaffected; heights derived through sin(P) carry this error."
